# NOTE: src/content/provenance.generated.json IS committed as of 2026-07-27.
# It was previously gitignored (regenerate-every-build), but that made the
# Vercel DEPLOY build hard-depend on full git history — and Vercel shallow-
# clones, so once real provenance blocks shipped (§12 PR 6), every deploy
# failed in the generator's shallow-clone guard. The committed artifact is
# regenerated + drift-checked in CI (full clone, `fetch-depth: 0`), so it can
# never go stale; the build falls back to it when git history is unavailable.
# See docs/provenance-model.md §5.2/§5.3.
#
# src/content/runs.generated.json is ALSO committed, same reasoning
# (docs/reports-surface.md §3.2/§6 PR 1) — it keeps Vercel's shallow clone
# working and is drift-checked in CI. It never needs the provenance
# artifact's git-history fallback (it is entirely git-free), but it is
# committed from day one to match the 2026-07-27 "commit the artifact"
# decision rather than re-litigating it per generated file.
